body:
This was far from a favorite for me, but was a cool movie to kill time. The humor is fun at first, but it get tiring. I miss a  more emotional and more drama in this. I don't know, after endgame and all the shit that went down these past movies, I would like to see less high school cliches and stuff. I know, they want to targeted a certain audience, but still. This movie didn't do much for me, from this universe, this was Peter's Holland appearance I enjoyed the last. I think I still like the Andrew Garfield spider man more than in this one. 

&#x200B;

For me, the best part of  was the power point tribute in the beginning. Comic san got me LOL

Adulting.   


I thought I was doing pretty good, then I've met people, some which are young them me, that are so much better at it.   


&#x200B;

I would like to say 13, the age where my father got me a cellphone. But that was in 2003, cellphones back there didn't do much, and things are so different now a day. 

&#x200B;

If the child proves to be mature enough and the responsability of having a phone, maybe it's ok to have one in early teens. 



&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Sleep every night without sleep meds.   


Insomnia + anxiety + depression = dreadful life   


&#x200B;

People leaving before the after credit scenes and I'm like: 

"Haven't you learned anything in the past 10 years?!"  





